Package: boswas-os
Architecture: all
Depends: boswas-branding (>= 1.0~alpha1),
         boswas-cli (>= 1.0~alpha3),
         boswas-compat (>= 1.0~alpha3),
         boswas-compat-manager (>= 1.0~alpha3),
         boswas-control-center (>= 1.0~alpha3),
         boswas-device-agent (>= 1.0~alpha3),
         boswas-security (>= 1.0~alpha1),
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Boswas OS release identity and core configuration
 Boswas OS is the Boswas Group company-managed desktop operating system.
 This package carries the Boswas OS release identity (/usr/lib/boswas/release
 and os-release: NAME="Boswas OS", ID=boswas, ID_LIKE=debian), the console
 banners, the device configuration under /etc/boswas (device.conf, read by
 the device agent), boot loader defaults, the live-session integration, and
 pulls in the other Boswas OS components.
 .
 base-files' os-release is diverted, and Debian's default console banners
 and message of the day are replaced; all are restored on removal.
 /etc/debian_version, ID_LIKE=debian and the package archive keep
 Debian tooling working; GRUB keeps Debian's EFI directory for Secure Boot.
